    "difficulty": "Mastery",
    "difficultyReason": "Recover colour counts and connect valid whole-number counts to the minimum possible total through divisibility."
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q21-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "A bag contains various coloured marbles. Some are red, some are blue, some are yellow and some are green. You are told that $P(\\text{red})=\\frac{1}{2}$, $P(\\text{blue})=\\frac{1}{4}$ and $P(\\text{yellow})=\\frac{1}{6}$.\n\nYou are not told the probability of selecting a green marble.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q21-a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "If there are 24 marbles:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p16-q21-a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Find how many marbles there are of each colour.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "12 red, 6 blue, 4 yellow and 2 green marbles.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Red}&=24\\times\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\\text{Red}&=12\\\\\\text{Blue}&=24\\times\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\\text{Blue}&=6\\\\\\text{Yellow}&=24\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\\\\\text{Yellow}&=4\\\\\\text{Green}&=24-12-6-4\\\\\\text{Green}&=2\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 12
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q21-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "What is the probability of getting a green marble?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{1}{12}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{green})&=\\frac{2}{24}\\\\P(\\text{green})&=\\frac{1}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q21-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "If there are 36 marbles:",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p16-q21-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Find how many marbles there are of each colour.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "18 red, 9 blue, 6 yellow and 3 green marbles.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Red}&=36\\times\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\\text{Red}&=18\\\\\\text{Blue}&=36\\times\\frac{1}{4}\\\\\\text{Blue}&=9\\\\\\text{Yellow}&=36\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\\\\\text{Yellow}&=6\\\\\\text{Green}&=36-18-9-6\\\\\\text{Green}&=3\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 12
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q21-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "What is the probability of getting a green marble?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{1}{12}$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{green})&=\\frac{3}{36}\\\\P(\\text{green})&=\\frac{1}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 14
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q21-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What is the minimum number of marbles in the bag?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "12 marbles.",
          "worked": "The total must be divisible by 2, 4 and 6 so that each colour has a whole number of marbles.\n\n$$\\operatorname{LCM}(2,4,6)=12$$\n\nWith 12 marbles there are 6 red, 3 blue, 2 yellow and 1 green, so the minimum is 12 marbles.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      }
    ]
  },
